      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62351ac81637aa52ab489144|full_name} I don't know the real reason why the game is blocked in France, but I can explain what I think, based on other similar cases.\n\nVRChat is a very open game, and it contains sensitive content (for example, related to sexuality) without mandatory age verification. However, French law is very strict on this point: any platform likely to expose minors to sensitive content must implement reliable verification.\n\nVRChat isn't the only case: several sites containing sensitive content have already been blocked in France for the same reason, because they didn't have a compliant age verification system.\n\nIn Spain and Germany, it seems to me that these sites aren't blocked, because the rules there are less strict.\n\nTherefore, in my opinion, this is the most likely reason why VRChat doesn't appear on the App Store in France.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
